course: dictionary
lesson: 2186
title: Cost: price and loss
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word cost has several jobs. As a verb it means to have a price: «Two apples cost 45 cents each.» As a noun, the cost is the price itself: «The total cost» is the amount you pay altogether.
explain: Cost can also mean to make you lose something. «Being late cost us the game» does not mean we paid money. It means we lost the game because we were late. Read the words around cost to see which meaning fits.
explain: To find the cost of many things, multiply the number by the price of one. Two apples at 45 cents each cost 2 × 45 = 90 cents. Then check your answer: does it make sense in the sentence?
fact: Cost means the price you must pay to get something.
fact: The cost of many things = the number × the price of one.
fact: «Costs 3 pounds each» means each one has a price of 3 pounds.
fact: «At all costs» means no matter what, whatever it takes.
fact: Fixed costs are bills that come every month, like rent, energy and council tax; they are paid before money goes on fun.
exercise: «Two apples cost 45 cents each.» What is the total cost of the two apples? | 45 cents | 100 cents | 10 cents | *90 cents
exercise: «A girl in Wales borrowed a library book and lost it; the fine and the cost of the book came out of her savings.» What does the cost of the book mean? | *The price of the book | The library's opening hours | Her favourite part of the story | The number of pages
exercise: «Being late cost us the game.» What does cost mean here? | We finished the game early | We bought the game | We were given the game for free | *We lost the game because of it
test: A pencil costs 35 pence. How much do 3 pencils cost? | 38 pence | *105 pence | 70 pence | 95 pence
test: «At all costs» means... | Very slowly and carefully | Never, not at all | Only if it is cheap | *No matter what
exam: «A smart meter shows how much energy the house is using right now and what it costs.» What does «what it costs» show families? | The number of rooms in the house | The weather outside | Which windows are open | *The price of the energy being used right now
